  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 110 PM EST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nWell defined upper low centered near Saginaw Bay (Lower MI) with \nseveral weak disturbances/troughs rotating around the feature as it \ndrifts slowly ESE reaching western NY by 12Z Sat. Weakly convergent \nflow along the eastern shores is keeping the main area of rain \nshowers from South Haven to South Bend. Instability and favorable \nfetch peak into mid afternoon with combination of lowering inversion \nheights, departing low and core of coldest air shifting east should \nlead to a downward trend into tonight. Kept some lingering pops into \nthe overnight before ending. Temperatures tonight will drop into the \nlow to mid 30s, coldest outside of any lake effect cloud cover.\n\nLow level WAA will commence on Saturday, but bulk of greatest \nincrease will occur in the afternoon, limiting impacts on afternoon \nhighs to the lower 50s. After one more cold night in the lower 30s, \nhigh temps will begin to rebound a few degrees each day into Tuesday \nwith a return to above normal levels (low to mid 60s) by Tuesday. \n\nA semi zonal upper flow will be interrupted by a northern stream \nwave, with a front pushing into the area by Wednesday. The trough \nwill deepen into the second half of the week with additional waves \nmove through the flow. The main impact appears to be a return to \nnear or somewhat below normal temperatures to end the work week. \nSome lake effect shower chances could arrive Thu/Fri, but overall \nflow right now may favor portions of far NW Indiana into NE \nIllinois.",
